# Plugin author orientation

You are working inside a scaffolded mySMB plugin project for `__SLUG__`. The user is building a marketplace plugin and wants you to help them author it.

## The deliverable lives in `plugin/`

That folder, and only that folder, is what eventually gets copied into the marketplace repo at `plugins/__SLUG__/`. Everything else (`harness/`, `node_modules/`, this skill folder) is local development scaffolding.

A complete plugin folder has:

```
plugin/
├── .claude-plugin/plugin.json     # manifest
├── .mcp.json                      # MCP server transport
├── README.md                      # MUST contain a ## Configuration section listing every ${VAR}
├── skills/<slug>-*.md             # slash-command instructions
├── agents/<slug>-*.md             # personas
├── widgets/<slug>-*.json          # dashboard tiles
└── widget-elements/
    ├── src/index.ts               # default-exports a PluginElementsModule
    └── dist/index.js              # COMMIT THIS — built artifact
```

The minimum legal plugin is `plugin.json` + `.mcp.json` + `README.md`. Everything else is optional. Add what the user actually needs.

## Which sister skill to load

| User says | Load this skill | Then |
|---|---|---|
| "add a widget" / "show this data on the dashboard" | `.claude/skills/composing-widgets/SKILL.md` | Write `plugin/widgets/__SLUG__-<name>.json`. |
| "add a helper" / "I need a `$computed` for X" | `.claude/skills/composing-widgets/SKILL.md` (decide: system vs plugin) → `.claude/skills/authoring-plugin-widget-elements/SKILL.md` (if plugin) | Add to `plugin/widget-elements/src/index.ts`, rebuild. |
| "what components / functions can I use?" | `.claude/skills/widget-elements-system/SKILL.md` | Pick from the catalog. |
| "add a slash command for X" | This skill — see "Skills" below. | Write `plugin/skills/__SLUG__-<task>.md`. |
| "add an assistant persona" | This skill — see "Agents" below. | Write `plugin/agents/__SLUG__-<name>.md`. |
| "wire up the MCP server" | This skill — see ".mcp.json" below. | Edit `plugin/.mcp.json`. |

## Skills

Each skill is a single `.md` file with frontmatter:

```markdown
---
name: __SLUG__-<task>
description: <one sentence — the model uses this to decide when to load the skill>
---

# Title

Imperative instructions in second person. Tell the model what to do, in what
order, and what NOT to do. Reference the MCP tools by name.
```

Filename = skill name. Always slug-prefix to prevent collisions across plugins.

## Agents

Same frontmatter shape, different content. An agent is a complete persona with goals, scope, and anti-scope. The "what you do NOT do" section is the load-bearing one — it stops the model from confidently hallucinating capabilities.

## .mcp.json

Three transports allowed: `stdio`, `sse`, `http`. Pick the highest preference:

1. Official upstream MCP servers on npm — launch with `npx -y <pkg>@latest`.
2. Official upstream remote MCP servers (sse / http).
3. Custom servers in this repo, with compiled `dist/` committed.

Every credential goes through `${VAR}` placeholders. Every `${VAR}` you reference must appear in `plugin/README.md` under a `## Configuration` heading — the marketplace validator enforces this.

`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` is reserved and expands to the plugin's absolute path at runtime. Use it instead of hardcoded paths.

## Testing locally

The harness in `harness/` is running on `http://localhost:5173`. It:

- Reads `plugin/widgets/*.json` and shows them in the sidebar.
- Reads `plugin/.mcp.json` and spawns each stdio server.
- Surfaces every server's tools in the bottom panel.
- Renders the selected widget on the right, with `__SLUG___<name>` `$computed` helpers wired up via the alias `@plugin-elements` → `../plugin/widget-elements/dist/index.js`.

So after you write or edit a widget, the user reloads the page and sees the change. After you edit `widget-elements/src/index.ts`, run `npm --prefix plugin/widget-elements run build` to refresh `dist/index.js` — the harness will pick it up on the next reload.

## When you're ready to ship

Tell the user to:

1. Copy `plugin/` to `mySMB-Plugin-Marketplace/Plugins/plugins/__SLUG__/`.
2. Add an entry to `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`.
3. From the marketplace root: `npx tsx scripts/validate.ts`.
4. Open a PR.
